-### [Surface SDF Loss](14235-surface-sdf-loss.md)
-A regularizer for Directional Distance Fields (DDF) that enforces consistency with a co-trained SDF by constraining DDF-reconstructed points to lie on the SDF's zero-level set.
-
-### [Geometry Loss](17091-geometry-loss.md)
-A composite regularization term incorporating multi-view geometric priors (depth, normals) and topological penalties (bubble loss) alongside SDF regression and Eikonal terms.
+TetraSDF Training Procedure optimizes a neural network to represent a signed distance field (SDF) using a multi-resolution tetrahedral grid, combining L1 regression, Eikonal regularization, and weight normalization constraints. It differs from standard MLP-based SDF training by utilizing a tetrahedral grid structure for spatial representation, which allows for efficient multi-resolution handling and specific mesh extraction via sub-polygonization.
